{
  "_readme": "GAME CONTENT, DRAFT PENDING PRODUCER REVIEW (every DisplayName and HerbariumEntry; no art yet: ArtKey is a placeholder key). The Wildgarden (docs/design/grove.md): PlotCount plots, each planted with one seed (Source shrine, gated by a discovery.json shrine's GroveUnlockId, or starter, unlocked from the first save); growth (GrowthHours, 3-24) is checked through OfflineClock. Cross-pollination is a curated, deterministic matrix, never rolled: CrossPollinations lists every (ParentA, ParentB) pair this content defines, order-independent, each naming its fixed ResultVarietyId; a self-pair (ParentA == ParentB) is what a lone plot of that seed harvests (GardenRules.Harvest), every other pair is what harvesting two different, ready plots together yields (GardenRules.HarvestPair) \u2014 every seed has exactly one self-pair, and every Varieties entry is reachable by some pair. A harvest deposits one of the resulting variety into the generic Grove item inventory (PlayerSave.Grove.Items) and records the herbarium find. Recipes (GardenRules.Craft) are deterministic (no rolls): they consume Grove item varieties and produce a decor unlock, a dye (a Grove item id \u2014 the seam a later PR spends for colour evolutions), or (not authored here yet) a cosmetic look. Validated by BeastCraft.Garden.GardenLibraryValidator (content load and the EditMode tests).",
